  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_0ea0a0e4310f44c68aec602822b603af",
      "statement": "A BFF Redis session is a five-field, tokenless record (`sessionId`, `userId`, `createdAt`, `lastActivityAt`, `expiresAt`) whose idle window, absolute lifetime, and per-user concurrency are tracked entirely independently of the Keycloak JWT's own expiry: `createSession()` sets `lastActivityAt = createdAt = now` and `expiresAt = now + env.sessionAbsoluteTimeoutMs`, so ending a session does not invalidate an already-issued JWT and an expired access token does not by itself end the session.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/bff-server/session-manager.ts#L28-L59",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ad6ca6bfdbf266b96b9cfb47916910f6e432fc7d1a950e5991ab8f7f2dda56b4:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/config/env.ts#L59-L62",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6a4fe55b103fd18aeb5c12234f2f4e1c9e285bff5b965bc9bfc1204ec504390b:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/types/auth.ts#L81-L87",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f13369f7e78b44687cdd3f71c971b5cae84b9e08b89f87300d79fd9f4b946dd4:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f5248830df3a4963a3ca3216260beb9c",
      "statement": "A session is stored under two Redis keys — `session:<sessionId>` (JSON, `SET ... EX <ttl>`) and `user-sessions:<userId>` (a set of that user's session IDs, maintained with `SADD`/`SREM` and given the same TTL) — and the TTL is a backstop derived from the session's remaining absolute lifetime (`sessionTtlSeconds`, floored at 1s), never a fixed value, so it can never be shorter than the configured idle/absolute policy. A corrupt or truncated stored value is treated as no session: `getSession()` deletes the bad key and returns null rather than throwing.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/bff-server/cache-service.ts#L20-L39",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:16934c8717227378b9260b8bd72bb016ecf588ba2f572dd6b62c812de31c5fc6:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/bff-server/cache-service.ts#L94-L120",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a111f64fabae41660706d388cf0c969829839d4de1ed56f8dc9098e37541015a:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/tests/integration/session-manager.integration.test.ts#L44-L56",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:260d8d7fa59ebf5b65011ba302c85b109bb50e355214785bd59bb3906714439c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_10ad382d3d9d41bcbcc443ceb1c5c90b",
      "statement": "`readLiveSession(sessionId)` is the session read authority and returns a discriminated union — `{ session }`, `{ expired: 'absolute' | 'idle'; userId }`, or `{ expired: 'missing' }` — checking the absolute timeout before the idle timeout, so a session past its maximum lifetime is reported as `absolute` even when it is also idle; it deletes the session on either expiry but not when the record is missing. `getValidSession()` still exists as a thin wrapper that collapses every non-live outcome to `null`, so only callers that must report *why* a session ended use `readLiveSession()`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/bff-server/session-manager.ts#L61-L96",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:45c078f2e1a01e75fa5839a233400f79edb15ab2df253b90572728403f723e4c:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/bff-server/unit-tests/session-manager.test.ts#L201-L231",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a2ac86837cf3191bba7e150926edf596e12ef108c35a9c4a3a0fd09708099e94:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_36cee0ff1fc242c0beae9229aab39e76",
      "statement": "`validateSessionTimeout()` (used by `/bff-api/auth/user`) maps each `readLiveSession` outcome to a distinct failure and audits the true reason: `missing` throws 401 `SESSION_NOT_FOUND` with no audit; `absolute` throws 401 `SESSION_ABSOLUTE_TIMEOUT` and audits `session_expired` with `reason: 'absolute'`; `idle` throws 401 `SESSION_IDLE_TIMEOUT` and audits `reason: 'idle'`; a live session is touched instead. A null session ID throws 401 `UNAUTHORIZED`. The refresh route, which still calls `getValidSession()`, cannot distinguish the two expiries and returns a single 401 `SESSION_EXPIRED` for both.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/app/bff-api/auth/refresh%2Bapi.ts#L40-L46",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fb27c711554cb68f215c3c8ac18927f6611aecc8c5a0fbd83dc5c83e6e7add04:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/bff-server/session-timeout.ts#L14-L48",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fc304a3683830bb761b8e3646411d4dc41af81ee4dd898e23d63bc7172dd7386:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/bff-server/unit-tests/session-timeout.test.ts#L44-L83",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3ea4c06e69862d718fd94c297ceca86c9f8cd61831ca8866ab5461f434610e37:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f201f4485eb34fca8d8327dc4406a9b4",
      "statement": "The idle window slides on exactly two routes — `/bff-api/auth/user` (via `validateSessionTimeout`, which calls `touchSession` on a live session) and `/bff-api/auth/refresh` (after its ownership check) — because `touchSession` has no other caller; domain routes authenticate the access-token JWT alone and never read the session record, so an idle session is caught at the next `/auth/user` or `/auth/refresh`. Feature 085 FR-013 corrected the earlier comments in `session-manager.ts` and `session-timeout.ts` that claimed enforcement on 'every authenticated request'.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/app/bff-api/auth/refresh%2Bapi.ts#L81-L81",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:29cb7b1b8ebf64be2211805faa63d4677b3a6fa1b46889efa2c75ab6361d0f9a:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/app/bff-api/auth/user%2Bapi.ts#L35-L43",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:46fa192b10918f17fe3006347b95f9fc75240bfda54956635bd6fbd5689bb778:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/bff-server/session-manager.ts#L98-L109",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:11fa58e4828794a65ae8197bb3e8d918f08143eab3d6a8d24ec3c4581850d42a:"
        },
        {
