    {
      "id": "claim_b0295b9f06b34ed4a50190daddc6ddfb",
      "statement": "`createSession()` enforces the per-user concurrent-session cap in two steps: a pre-add count check that evicts when the count is already at or above `MAX_SESSIONS`, then, after the new session is cached, a trim loop that re-reads the count and keeps evicting while it exceeds the cap. The loop's no-progress guard (`if (next >= count) break`) exists because the `user-sessions:<userId>` set can retain members whose `session:` object is already gone, and `evictOldestSession()` returns early when no valid session is found — without the break the loop could spin without the count ever falling. The post-add trim is what makes the cap hold under simultaneous logins, since the pre-add check alone is TOCTOU-racy (feature 009 FR-018).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/bff-server/session-manager.ts#L28-L59",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ad6ca6bfdbf266b96b9cfb47916910f6e432fc7d1a950e5991ab8f7f2dda56b4:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/bff-server/unit-tests/session-manager.test.ts#L296-L324",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3b4c4fb09fa7af6a324046a4e8bbb1fe0ef4f1e515dd69c57c44352cffc36bc7:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/tests/integration/concurrent-session-cap.integration.test.ts#L30-L38",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3fe09da683313b33d6d9d2526245a39c24c8a95b9a7ba679afc0122cc0bb2d63:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_97b80e2fc1204db989f11b713728030a",
      "statement": "Eviction removes the valid session with the smallest `lastActivityAt` (sort ascending, take the first) — the least-recently-active session, which is not necessarily the oldest by `createdAt` — and `MAX_SESSIONS` is bound once at module load from `env.maxConcurrentSessions` (`MAX_CONCURRENT_SESSIONS`, default 10), so changing the environment variable after the module is imported has no effect.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/bff-server/session-manager.ts#L128-L143",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b90123ff985973d4d748e651b4eeed33b2f40251fd3eaca1d45ed6abb52b7a9e:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/bff-server/session-manager.ts#L19-L19",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:36c3ba60765e5c6e16f214f19fc642fff3688dd4e78d2c707d4253044b64ac9a:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/config/env.ts#L62-L62",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:62851eb1792183253f06bca367170eae964c8f9eda59a2bf799d851aa101e444:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_14638147ab594c6f9dee2c6b6e45b8a1",
      "statement": "Every eviction emits `logger.audit('session_evicted', { userId, activeSessions, maxSessions })`, where `activeSessions` counts only the sessions that still resolved rather than the raw set cardinality, and the evicted session ID is deliberately not logged in any form — under the key name `sessionId` the logger would redact it to a constant while still tripping the `mcm-no-token-logging` SAST rule, and any other key name would leak it (feature 052 FR-001/FR-004).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/bff-server/session-manager.ts#L145-L160",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:874988026328e902b523bc6197f3baf9b527d2b1089588af6f91eb382cf5795b:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/tests/integration/concurrent-session-cap.integration.test.ts#L40-L82",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c80d3558563429b66763fa5c5737386222845edafa3b73e0c0aa216c050aaf08:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4fbec41f62ca4f40ad98144545b1cb73",
      "statement": "Nothing in `session-manager.ts` verifies that a session ID belongs to the caller — ownership is enforced at the route boundary by all three session-touching routes: `auth/user+api.ts` authenticates before any session side effect and calls `validateSessionTimeout` only when `session.userId === payload.sub`; `auth/logout+api.ts` terminates only when the resolved session's `userId` matches the token subject; and `auth/refresh+api.ts` (feature 085 US2, item #607, FR-006/FR-007) validates the subject of the access token minted from the client-supplied refresh credential against `session.userId` before touching the session, and on a mismatch revokes the just-minted refresh token, terminates the session, audits `session_refresh_owner_mismatch`, clears the auth cookies, and returns 401 `SESSION_OWNER_MISMATCH` without extending anything or issuing a credential.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/app/bff-api/auth/logout%2Bapi.ts#L28-L55",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8868369fd1a086a9719d132b3d660a2fd0aba918a34b8cc909fa2c34cc049504:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/app/bff-api/auth/refresh%2Bapi.ts#L61-L79",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fdadf6a9ced9a632ae209aa6106883efbf7e73ca2ce254f0cb63eac412edc374:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/app/bff-api/auth/user%2Bapi.ts#L29-L43",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cf91cf1ab8e07bdfdaa371398e39739199f89d8bc9bbbff8171d6660cfeb2c5d:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/tests/integration/auth-session-side-effects.integration.test.ts#L38-L72",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:901a184cbe069604e2de6f8e0257378ecd9701776964305af50fc52846ae8802:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_44eeddbe45a8494f892b1cd2e18e43bd",
      "statement": "The client holds only the opaque session ID, never a token: on web nothing is persisted client-side (the BFF's `HttpOnly` cookies are the source of truth), and on native only the opaque ID is stored in SecureStore under `mcm_session_id` as a startup hydration hint for `hasStoredSession()`, which `AuthProvider` always follows with a `/bff-api/auth/user` call before treating the user as authenticated. The ID reaches the client as both the `mcm_session_id` `HttpOnly; SameSite=Strict` cookie and the `X-Session-Id` response header on login; subsequent requests are authenticated by the access-token cookie, though the BFF still accepts `Authorization: Bearer` ahead of the cookie.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/app/bff-api/auth/login%2Bapi.ts#L121-L124",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7ec93f3573423897860f7e3c59d6669acedebcd0d07b117e86c85422f4aa11d7:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://frontend/mcm-app/src/bff-server/auth.ts#L36-L55",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d5cc694fac71924ea90a67e2838846b8246b59ac87e76eae815ad9239fe1c564:"
        },
        {
